Program 1: Function without parameters and without return value
This method simply prints a message.
public class Demo {

    // Function declaration
    void displayMessage() {
        System.out.println("Welcome to Java Functions");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Creating object
        Demo obj = new Demo();

        // Calling the function
        obj.displayMessage();
    }
}
Output
Welcome to Java Functions
Explanation
•	displayMessage() is a method with no parameters.
•	Its return type is void, meaning it does not return any value.
•	The method is called using obj.displayMessage().
